# Site Reviewer Agent

Before **UI, dashboard, navigation, intake, or messaging** changes:

1. Read [`.aod-context/strategy/AssociateOnDemand_Master_Implementation_Roadmap.md`](../../.aod-context/strategy/AssociateOnDemand_Master_Implementation_Roadmap.md) (Phase 1 for current UX).
2. Read [`.aod-context/strategy/AssociateOnDemand_Deep_UX_Audit.md`](../../.aod-context/strategy/AssociateOnDemand_Deep_UX_Audit.md).
3. Read [`.aod-context/agent/AssociateOnDemand_Site_Reviewer_Agent_Instructions.md`](../../.aod-context/agent/AssociateOnDemand_Site_Reviewer_Agent_Instructions.md).
4. Follow the checklist in [`docs/runbooks/site-reviewer-agent.md`](../../docs/runbooks/site-reviewer-agent.md).

## Checklist (must not regress)

- **Relief / capacity** — not stress-first metrics or “marketplace” language
- **Navigation** — primary: Dashboard, New assignment, Inbox, Matters, Templates; secondary collapsed
- **Firm Memory** — `/firm-memory` (also Settings → Firm Memory) + dashboard CTA when empty
- **No false Stripe** — Phase 0 offline invoicing copy only
- **Overflow journey** — 4-step Getting Started (Firm Memory → Assignment → Assessment → Review)
- **Associate panel** — matter + deliverable context; “What would you like RMV to work on?”

## Do not rebuild (verify shipped)

Firm Memory wizard, Documents assessment upload, AOS discretionary facts, sample discount, Phase 0 billing honesty.

## Persona lock

Build **overflow counsel / capacity relief** for external firms; RMV verifies year one. Associate marketplace is Phase 3+ only.
